{
  "slug": "gimme-the-lint",
  "name": "Gimme The Lint",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Progressive linting system that only blocks on new violations, never on legacy code. Baselines existing lint issues by directory, then enforces clean code going forward. Supports Python (Ruff) and JavaScript/TypeScript (ESLint) in monorepo configurations. Includes drift detection, auto-healing, git hooks, and a GitHub Action for CI enforcement. Directory-chunked baselines allow gradual adoption without a big-bang cleanup.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 agent**, **8 commands** and **1 hook**.\n\n- **Agents** (1): `linting-agent` (Runs progressive linting and entity-contract checks via gimme-the-lint and reports violations)\n- **Commands** (8): `contract` (Check whether your data model agrees with the schemas that expose it (entity-contract drift)), `lint-baseline` (Create or refresh progressive-lint baselines (captures existing violations so only NEW ones block future commits)), `lint-status` (Show the progressive linting dashboard — per-app baseline status and drift detection), `lint` (Run progressive linting checks on the current project (only NEW violations above the baseline are flagged)), `policy` (Get or set the gimme-the-lint update policy (auto | nudge | off)), `relink` (Re-run the skill linker — refresh symlinks from node_modules into .claude/skills/), `status` (Show installed version, latest available version, current update policy, and hook registration state), `update` (Update gimme-the-lint to the latest version (runs npm update + re-links skills))\n- **Hooks** (1): `SessionStart`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install gimme-the-lint@claude-community` from `TheGlitchKing/gimme-the-lint`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "agent": 1,
    "hook": 1,
    "command": 8
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
  "author": {
    "name": "TheGlitchKing"
  },
